# Probe 39 (scripts/probe_hierarchy_matrix_slicer.py): a model hierarchy in a matrix's Rows and a slicer's Field, the one reason those two wells refused one.
# Seen (the user built Desktop's own matrix and slicer by hand, expanded both candidates, then refreshed and saved; all three STEPS.md steps landed in one save, so they are one step here): dragging the hierarchy Geography into a matrix's Rows and a slicer's Field showed "Geography" as a root with Country and Region under it in both wells. Desktop's own matrix writes one HierarchyLevel projection per level in Rows, in level order, the shape probe 16 recorded, with Country "active": true and Region "active": false — an explicit false on the deeper level, not an omission. Its own slicer writes both levels in Values with "active": true on each, as probe 20 recorded for two plain columns. Blueprint's candidates equal those projections exactly, key for key, in both wells: the save left the candidate slicer untouched entirely and changed the candidate matrix only by flipping Region to "active": true (the user had expanded it; Desktop's own unexpanded matrix kept false) and adding expansionStates at visual.expansionStates, never rewriting a field. Note the candidate matrix's flags are render's own column-chart output, while the candidate slicer's every-level-active was set by the probe, so a slicer hierarchy needs a render change too. Both drew: the matrix shows FR/UK with expanders (FR -> East 150, West 50; total 500) and the slicer shows Country, Region with FR and UK expanding to their regions. The save also bumped $schema 2.13.0 -> 2.14.0 on the files it rewrote and added Desktop's condition-less auto filterConfig to the control column chart. All content invented.

